title: fortify_complete
---

Narrator:
The reinforcement completes on schedule.

---

Narrator:
Additional garrison. Resupply lines secured. Overlapping patrol routes confirmed.

The system is harder to move now.

---

Narrator:
Not because it's impregnable.

Nothing is impregnable.

---

Narrator:
Because the cost of taking it just went up.

---

<<if $remaining_strength > 10>>
    Narrator:
    The numbers look solid.

    Narrator:
    Whoever comes for this system will need to commit more than they'd like to.

    Narrator:
    That buys time.

    Narrator:
    Time is what you're actually purchasing here.

<<else>>
    Narrator:
    It's lighter than ideal.

    Narrator:
    But it's something.

    Narrator:
    The difference between a system that falls in minutes and one that holds for hours can decide everything.

<<endif>>

---

Narrator:
You file the defensive upgrade.

The log accepts it without event.

---

Narrator:
Good.

---

-> [Acknowledge]

===

title: fortify_commit
---
Narrator: Reinforcement order confirmed.

The fleet digs in. Positions hardened, supply lines secured, defences layered against the next contact.

Hold until told otherwise.
===
